  "notes": [
    "Box size is sqrt(w*h) of the YOLO label, in native pixels and after scaling by imgsz / max(w, h), the long-side resize Ultralytics applies before letterboxing (val) or mosaic (train). Train-time scale augmentation (scale=0.5 -> x0.5..x1.5) spreads this further.",
    "8 px = one stride-8 cell of the P3 head (the finest feature map in YOLO26 and YOLOv8); 16 / 32 px = P4 / P5 strides; 32 px also equals COCO's 'small' area threshold (32^2) when applied at native resolution.",
    "Labels exclude VisDrone ignored regions (score 0), as in Ultralytics' VisDrone.yaml converter."
  ]
